      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "λ = 0   →   correction off; raw_synthetic propagates (this is the collapsing baseline)\nλ = 1   →   z' = T(z); every sample snapped onto the anchor manifold (near-arrests collapse)\n0 < λ < 1   →   partial pull of each sample toward the real-anchor manifold",
      "rawText": "λ = 0   →   correction off; raw_synthetic propagates (this is the collapsing baseline)\nλ = 1   →   z' = T(z); every sample snapped onto the anchor manifold (near-arrests collapse)\n0 < λ < 1   →   partial pull of each sample toward the real-anchor manifold",
      "originalText": "λ = 0   →   correction off; raw_synthetic propagates (this is the collapsing baseline)\nλ = 1   →   z' = T(z); every sample snapped onto the anchor manifold (near-arrests collapse)\n0 < λ < 1   →   partial pull of each sample toward the real-anchor manifold",
